% The Logical English twin of an s(CASP) program, written by the s(CASP) translator
% (InsurLE2/migration/scasp) from loanwithcure-scasp.pl (kept in sources/).
% Every expected answer in the scenarios is s(CASP)'s own answer on the source.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a date* is on or before *a second date*.
    *a person* has *an obligation*.
    *an obligation* is that *a description*.
    *a borrower* defaults on *a date*.
    *a borrower* cures the failure of *an obligation* onorbefore *a date*.
    *a borrower* fails on *a date* to fulfil *an obligation*.
    *a lender* notifies *a borrower* on *a date* that *a message*.
    *a borrower* pays *an amount* to *a lender* on *a date*.
    the loan is accelerated on *a date*.

the knowledge base loanwithcure includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/loanwithcure-scasp.pl".

a date is on or before a second date if
    the second date is a number N days after the date
    and N >= 0.

the_borrower has obligation1.

obligation1 is that the_borrower pays 550 to the_lender on 2015-06-01.

the_borrower has obligation2.

obligation2 is that the_borrower pays 525 to the_lender on 2016-06-01.

the_borrower defaults on a date if
    the_borrower has an obligation
    and the_borrower fails on a second date to fulfil the obligation
    and the_lender notifies the_borrower on a third date that the_borrower fails on the second date to fulfil the obligation
    and the date is 2 days after the third date
    and it is not the case that the_borrower cures the failure of the obligation onorbefore the date.

the_borrower cures the failure of an obligation onorbefore a date if
    the obligation is that the_borrower pays an amount to the_lender on a second date
    and the_borrower pays the amount to the_lender on a third date
    and the_borrower notifies the_lender on a fourth date that the_borrower pays the amount to the_lender on the third date
    and the third date is on or before the date
    and the fourth date is on or before the date.

the_borrower fails on a date to fulfil an obligation if
    the obligation is that the_borrower pays an amount to the_lender on the date
    and it is not the case that the_borrower pays the amount to the_lender on the date.

scenario payment is, as stated in the source program at scenario payment:
    the_lender notifies the_borrower on 2016-06-04 that the_borrower fails on 2016-06-01 to fulfil obligation2.
    the_borrower pays 525 to the_lender on 2016-06-05.
    the_borrower notifies the_lender on 2016-06-06 that the_borrower pays 525 to the_lender on 2016-06-05.
